<.shell title="Icons" current={:icons}>
  <h1>Icons</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Heroicons, the set the app already uses. A small, fixed list: an icon helps people find or
    recognize something, and never replaces the words.
  </p>

  <h2>The set</h2>
  <p>Use only these. To use a new icon, add it to this list with its use first.</p>
  <.table id="icon-set" rows={icons()}>
    <:col :let={{_name, micro, _mini, _outline, _use}} label="16" class="w-px">
      <.icon name={micro} class="size-4" />
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, _micro, mini, _outline, _use}} label="20" class="w-px">
      <.icon name={mini} class="size-5" />
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, _micro, _mini, outline, _use}} label="24" class="w-px">
      <.icon name={outline} class="size-6" />
    </:col>
    <:col
      :let={{name, _micro, _mini, _outline, _use}}
      label="Name"
      class="w-px mono whitespace-nowrap"
    >
      {name}
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, _micro, _mini, _outline, use}} label="Use">{use}</:col>
  </.table>

  <h2>Sizes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>16, solid</strong>: beside sm text: breadcrumbs, back links, pagination, small buttons, chips.
    </li>
    <li><strong>20, solid</strong>: beside md text: buttons, banner titles, toasts.</li>
    <li><strong>24, outline</strong>: on its own line, such as warning text.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In use</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.form_actions>
      <.button href="#">
        Open in D4H <.icon name="hero-arrow-top-right-on-square-micro" class="size-4" />
      </.button>
      <.button><.icon name="hero-arrow-path-mini" class="size-5" /> Refresh from D4H</.button>
      <.button size={:sm} href="#">
        <.icon name="hero-arrow-down-tray-micro" class="size-4" /> Download PDF
      </.button>
    </.form_actions>
  </div>

  <h2>Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      An icon sits beside words. The only icon without words is the close or remove ×, and it has an <code>aria-label</code>.
    </li>
    <li>At most one icon per button. It leads, except the external-link icon, which trails.</li>
    <li>
      Only the uses listed above. No icons beside headings, in table cells, or for decoration.
    </li>
    <li>Icons take the text colour. Banners and toasts colour theirs to match.</li>
    <li>
      In the app: <code>&lt;.icon name="hero-chevron-left-micro" /&gt;</code>
      for 16, <code>-mini</code>
      for 20, and no suffix for 24.
    </li>
  </ul>
</.shell>
